---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../data/services';
import counterImg from '../assets/images/scripts-in-counter.jpg';
const service = serviceBySlug('medication-packing')!;
const emailHref = `mailto:${site.emailPharmacy}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Webster pack enquiry')}`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does medication packing cost?', a: 'Medication packing is free for concession and health care card holders, and $5 a week for everyone else. Call us or ask at the prescription counter to get started.' },
  { q: 'What is a Webster pack?', a: 'A Webster pack is a weekly blister pack. Each dose is sealed in its own compartment and labelled with the day and time it should be taken, so you can see at a glance what has and hasn’t been taken. Ask us if you’d like to see one.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to book to start medication packing?', a: 'No. Call us on ' + site.phone + ' or ask at the prescription counter at the back of the store, and bring in your current medicines and prescriptions.' },
  { q: 'Can a family member or carer collect my packs?', a: 'Yes. Tell us who else can collect packs or talk to us about your medicines, and we’ll note it on your profile.' },
  { q: 'What happens if my doctor changes my medicines?', a: 'Bring or send us the new prescription as soon as possible. We’ll update your packs and let you know when the new ones are ready. Please don’t push tablets out or add them to a pack yourself.' },
  { q: 'Are Webster packs free for pensioners?', a: 'Yes, if you have a concession card. Packing is free for concession and health care card holders, including Pensioner Concession Card holders, and $5 a week for everyone else.' },
  { q: 'Can I start by email?', a: `Yes. Email ${site.emailPharmacy} with your name (or the name of the person you care for), a phone number and a list or photos of the current medicines, and we’ll call you to set up the packs.` },
  { q: 'Do I need to bring my prescriptions?', a: 'Yes, to start. Bring in your current medicines and prescriptions, or ask your doctor to send your scripts straight to us. A pharmacist checks every medicine, dose and timing before we set up your packs.' },
];
---

<ServicePage
  service={service}
  title="Webster Packs Broadbeach, Free for Concession | Priceline"
  description="Weekly Webster packs at Priceline Pacific Fair, Broadbeach, Gold Coast. Free for concession and health care card holders, $5 a week otherwise. No appointment needed."
  h1="Medication packing (Webster packs) at Pacific Fair"
  lead="Yes, Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair in Broadbeach offers medication packing: your medicines sorted into weekly blister packs (Webster packs), with every dose labelled by day and time and checked by a pharmacist. It’s free for concession and health care card holders, and $5 a week otherwise. No appointment is needed; call us, email us or ask at the prescription counter."
  faqs={faqs}
  primaryCta={{ label: `Call ${site.phone}`, href: site.phoneHref, event: 'cta_call' }}
  secondaryCta={{ label: 'Email us to get started', href: emailHref, event: 'cta_email' }}
  dateModified="2026-10-25"
>
  <h2>How much does medication packing cost?</h2>
  <Image src={counterImg} alt="The scripts-in counter at the Priceline Pharmacy Pacific Fair dispensary, where medication packs are set up and collected" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px" />
  <p>Medication packing is <strong>free for concession and health care card holders</strong>, and $5 a week for everyone else.</p>

  <h2>How does medication packing work?</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Talk to us.</strong> Bring in your current medicines and prescriptions, or ask your doctor to send scripts to us.</li>
    <li><strong>We set up your profile.</strong> A pharmacist checks every medicine, dose and timing, and flags anything that needs a question to your doctor.</li>
    <li><strong>We pack your medicines.</strong> Each week’s medicines are sealed into a blister pack labelled with the day and time of each dose.</li>
    <li><strong>You collect.</strong> Pick up your packs each week, or have a family member or carer collect for you.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Who is medication packing for?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>People taking several medicines at different times of day</li>
    <li>Anyone who sometimes forgets whether they’ve taken a dose</li>
    <li>Older people living independently</li>
    <li>Family members and carers managing medicines for someone else</li>
    <li>Anyone whose medicines change often after hospital visits or specialist appointments</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Setting up Webster packs for Mum or Dad?</h2>
  <p>Blister packs make it easy to see at a glance whether today’s doses have been taken, which gives you peace of mind if you don’t live with the person you care for. You can get it started for them, even if you live out of town:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Get in touch.</strong> Call us on <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>, or email <a href={emailHref}>{site.emailPharmacy}</a> with their name, a phone number and a list or photos of their current medicines.</li>
    <li><strong>Sort out the scripts.</strong> Ask their doctor to send the scripts straight to us. If they need a GP, <a href="/help-medical/">Help Medical</a> is an independent general practice located inside our store.</li>
    <li><strong>Tell us who can help.</strong> With their OK, we’ll note who else can collect packs or talk to us about their medicines.</li>
    <li><strong>Collect each week.</strong> They, you or another family member or carer can pick up the packs.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Packing is free for concession and health care card holders, including Pensioner Concession Card holders.</p>

  <h2>Family visiting the Gold Coast?</h2>
  <p>Over Christmas and the school holidays, lots of parents and grandparents come to stay for a few weeks. If someone staying with you usually has Webster packs, we can pack their medicines while they’re here. Bring in their medicines and scripts a few days before they need their first pack. If their scripts are kept at their usual pharmacy, see <a href="/transfer-prescriptions-new-pharmacy/">how to move prescriptions to a new pharmacy</a>.</p>

  <h2>What happens when a medicine changes?</h2>
  <p>If a doctor changes a dose or adds a new medicine, bring or send us the new script as soon as possible. We’ll update the packs and let you know when the new ones are ready. Please don’t try to push tablets out or add them yourself.</p>

  <h2>How do I get started?</h2>
  <p>Call us on <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>, email <a href={emailHref}>{site.emailPharmacy}</a> or ask at the prescription counter at the back of the store. If you take several medicines, a free <a href="/medication-reviews/">medication review</a> with one of our pharmacists is a good first step, and we can keep your repeat <a href="/prescriptions/">prescriptions on file</a> so you don’t need to bring the paperwork each week.</p>
</ServicePage>
